      "itemDescription": "The off-price department store chain brought in nearly $3.5 billion in profits in 2022, a 7% increase over 2021. TJX dropped 12 spots on the Fortune 500 list after a 22-spot jump last year.<br />\r\n<ul><br />\r\n \t<li>Marmaxx, TJX\u2019s apparel unit, was its biggest revenue driver, bringing in $30 billion of the $49.9 billion the company generated overall. Its HomeGoods division, however, saw slower sales after two years of expansion during the pandemic.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>TJX continues to lag in the e-commerce space, which held the company back at COVID\u2019s height.</li><br />\r\n \t<li>Still, TJX has outlasted many of its competitors; Bed Bath &amp; Beyond\u2019s bankruptcy may lead to more foot traffic at TJX stores.</li><br />\r\n</ul>",
