      "image": null,
      "itemDescription": "<span data-sheets-value=\"{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:&quot;TJX took a particularly brutal beating from the pandemic last year, hit by the double whammy of having almost no e-commerce to fall back on when its stores were closed for long periods, and the precipitous drop in spending on fashion. Sales fell 23% to $32.1 billion\u2014but the damage could have been worse. For one thing TJX\u2019s HomeGoods business slipped only 4%. And when its other banners, T.J. Maxx and Marshalls, reopened, business rebounded quickly. There are signs of pent-up demand for fashion apparel that should give TJX a boost this year (barring any new outbreaks that close stores en masse again), and spending on the home continues apace.&quot;}\" data-sheets-userformat=\"{&quot;2&quot;:14723,&quot;3&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:0},&quot;4&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:16777215},&quot;10&quot;:2,&quot;11&quot;:4,&quot;14&quot;:{&quot;1&quot;:2,&quot;2&quot;:0},&quot;15&quot;:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;16&quot;:11}\">TJX took a particularly brutal beating from the pandemic last year, hit by the double whammy of having almost no e-commerce to fall back on when its stores were closed for long periods, and the precipitous drop in spending on fashion. Sales fell 23% to $32.1 billion\u2014but the damage could have been worse. For one thing TJX\u2019s HomeGoods business slipped only 4%. And when its other banners, T.J. Maxx and Marshalls, reopened, business rebounded quickly. There are signs of pent-up demand for fashion apparel that should give TJX a boost this year (barring any new outbreaks that close stores en masse again), and spending on the home continues apace.</span>",
      "uri": "/ranking/global500/2021/",
      "__typename": "_ItemRankingListsType"
