        "__typename": "rankingListItemImage"
      },
      "itemDescription": "The off-price discount fashion and home goods retailer continued its long march toward retail dominance, with sales up 7% in 2019, to $41.7 billion, making it bigger than Macy\u2019s and J.C. Penney combined. In the early days of the pandemic, TJX revenues fell off nearly entirely, with all stores closed and only a tiny e-commerce business in operation. But coming out of the lockdowns, TJX's strong financials should make its stores even more desirable to fashion brands as department stores continue to wither, analysts say. What\u2019s more, TJX\u2019s home furnishings chain HomeGoods has been booming alongside the more apparel-oriented T.J. Maxx and Marshalls.",
